TI  - Assessment of an international breaststroke swimmer using a race readiness test.
PG  - 139-43
AB  - Competitive swimmers routinely undertake a 7 x 200-m incremental step test to 
      evaluate their fitness and readiness to compete.An exercise protocol more closely 
      replicating competition swimming speeds may provide further insight into the 
      swimmer's physiological and technical readiness for competition. This case study 
      reports data over a 3-year period from 11 Race Readiness Tests, which were 
      completed, in addition to the 7 x 200-m test, as an attempt to provide the 
      swimmer and coach with a fuller assessment. For this individual, data provided 
      objective information from which to assess training status and race readiness 
      following a transition from 200-m to 100-m race training. Data also raised a 
      question as to whether a 100-m maximal effort 10 minutes before another one 
      actually enhances performance owing to a priming effect.
