TI  - Analysis and processing of heart rate variability by time-frequency 
      representation: quantification of the pedaling frequency modulation.
PG  - 5-8
LID - 10.1109/IEMBS.2009.5332621 [doi]
AB  - It has been shown that a pedaling frequency component can be extracted from the 
      heart rate variability (HRV) signal using a time-varying filter. It is shown that 
      this filter can be implemented directly in the time-frequency plane with 
      different approaches. The need of resampling the data is also discussed with 
      regard to the artifacts produced when the shanon condition is not fulfilled. In 
      order to interpret the similar amplitude profiles of the pedaling component for 
      untrained and trained subjects, an attempt for the model parameters setting is 
      proposed. Consistent results on a large data set illustrate the feasibility of 
      such processing.
