TI  - Comparison of the Physical Response During Official Matches and Small-Sided Games 
      in International Cerebral Palsy Footballers: Implications for Evidence-Based 
      Classification.
PG  - 4-18
LID - 10.1123/apaq.2021-0206 [doi]
AB  - This study aimed to analyze whether there are differences and associations in the 
      physical responses in international-level cerebral palsy footballers between 
      official matches and 2v2 small-sided games (2v2-SSG). One hundred seventy 
      international cerebral palsy footballers participated in this study during three 
      international championships. The physical responses of mean and maximum 
      velocities, total distance, distance covered at different intensities, short-term 
      actions, and player load were collected during 2v2-SSG and the real competition. 
      The mean velocity, total distance, jogging, medium- and high-intensity distances, 
      the number of moderate/high accelerations, decelerations, and player load were 
      relatively higher in the 2v2-SSG than in the official matches. Even though the 
      2v2-SSG could become an appropriate drill to include during the classification 
      process, due to the differences between a 2v2-SSG and the official competition, 
      it is necessary to deepen the scientific knowledge for developing observation 
      methods during real competition to strengthen the relationships between eligible 
      impairments and activity limitation.
