TI  - [Testosterone deficiency related to "relative energy deficiency in sport"].
LID - V10240674 [pii]
LID - 10.61409/V10240674 [doi]
AB  - In this case report, a 29-year-old formerly healthy man presented with fatigue, 
      reduced libido, and erectile dysfunction. He had lost 12 kg due to extensive 
      training and disordered eating. Blood tests showed hypogonadotropic hypogonadism, 
      low insulin-like growth factor-1, and anaemia. His condition was due to 
      functional testosterone deficiency related to "relative energy in sport" (RED-S). 
      Symptoms and testosterone levels improved following reduction in training load 
      and weight gain, underscoring the importance of addressing energy imbalance 
      rather than opting for testosterone therapy in this condition.
