VI  - 2006
DP  - 2006
TI  - Relationships between muscle activity and autonomic regulation during cycling 
      with a torque-assisted bicycle.
PG  - 2702-5
AB  - For customizing the assistance scheme of a torque-assisted bicycle, we estimated 
      physical activity during cycling with ECG and surface EMG for the circuit 
      including a steep uphill section near the middle and compared it with the vehicle 
      data. Using the respiratory-sinus-arrhythmia-related power ratio in the 
      fluctuation of the R-R interval, prRSA and a muscular fatigue index, we 
      classified physical activity into four groups for each trial. Results showed that 
      the assist enlarged prRSA but did not sufficiently support muscular fatigue.
