SB  - IM
OAB - Cardiac troponins are blood biomarkers that are used to assess the presence of 
      damage to the heart. Exercise can raise cardiac troponin levels in recreational 
      athletes without symptoms of heart problems. We aimed to determine the prevalence 
      and predictors of cardiac troponin elevations following exercise, and present the 
      following findings: Exercise leads to cardiac troponin elevations with abnormal 
      values in more than one in three athletes.These elevations were most common with 
      high-sensitivity assays, cTnT measurements, in middle aged athletes, and after 
      endurance sports with a duration of 3-6 hours.Sex and training status did not 
      influence the likelihood of post-exercise troponin elevations.
