TI  - Carbohydrate availability and training adaptation: effects on cell metabolism.
PG  - 152-60
LID - 10.1097/JES.0b013e3181f44dd9 [doi]
AB  - Several markers of endurance training adaptation are enhanced to a greater extent 
      when individuals undertake selected training sessions with low compared with 
      normal muscle glycogen content or with low exogenous carbohydrate availability. 
      The potential mechanisms underlying the cellular responses arising from such 
      nutrient-exercise interactions are discussed in the context of promoting training 
      adaptation.
