IS  - 0301-5548 (Linking)
VI  - 64
IP  - 5
DP  - 1992
TI  - Respiratory sinus arrhythmia alteration following training in endurance athletes.
PG  - 434-6
AB  - Significant increases in maximum oxygen consumption (VO2max) were noted in nine 
      young track athletes following an 8-week high-intensity running period (P less 
      than 0.05). VO2max was measured, prior to and following the training program, 
      using an on-line, open-circuit spirometry system. Parasympathetic activity was 
      assessed using heart period variation (R-R interval in milliseconds) during 
      carefully controlled breathing activity (R sinus arrhythmia). Following the 
      training program, a 7.3% increase in aerobic capacity was associated with a 23.1% 
      augmentation of efferent parasympathetic activity (P less than 0.01). These data 
      suggest that enhanced aerobic capacity increases efferent parasympathetic tone.
