OAB - Athletes’ heart adaptations include changes in cardiac tissue composition, but 
      the link between fitness and cardiac magnetic resonance mapping is not fully 
      understood. This study explores how cardiorespiratory fitness, assessed with 
      cardiopulmonary exercise testing, correlates with cardiac structure and T1/T2 
      mapping values in elite athletes.Higher cardiorespiratory fitness is associated 
      with larger cardiac volumes and mass and lower T1 and T2 mapping values.Our 
      results suggest that the observed moderately lower T1 values in athletes may 
      reflect physiological adaptation.
